From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Norman Herms <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 15:25:12 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] drm/sun4i: sun6i_mipi_dsi: Clean up the encoder and connector
 on unbind

sun4i_drv no longer calls drm_mode_config_cleanup() itself (drm/sun4i:
drv: Do not call drm_mode_config_cleanup()). The managed release of
drm_mode_config_init() destroys the mode objects at the last
drm_dev_put() instead, after component_unbind_all(), and, while
userspace still holds the device open, after the display engine device
has released its devres.

The DSI encoder and connector are embedded in struct sun6i_dsi, which is
allocated at probe and freed when the device is removed, and they are
destroyed through their .destroy hooks, so they are cleaned up on freed
memory if userspace holds the device open while the DSI device is
removed.

Clean them up in the unbind callback of the component, as sun4i_tv does,
while the memory is certainly alive. The bind error path already does
the same for the encoder. This has to come after the removal of the
explicit call in sun4i_drv, which would have cleaned them up a second
time.

Not covered: the tear down of the DSI host, which stays in remove.

Tested on Radxa Cubie A7S: not tested; the board has no controller of
this kind, the code is compiled only.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c
index d504ae583294..a213ccee2e52 100644
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/sun4i/sun6i_mipi_dsi.c
@@ -1100,6 +1100,8 @@ static void sun6i_dsi_unbind(struct device *dev, struct device *master,
 	struct sun6i_dsi *dsi = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 
 	dsi->drm = NULL;
+	drm_connector_cleanup(&dsi->connector);
+	drm_encoder_cleanup(&dsi->encoder);
 }
 
 static const struct component_ops sun6i_dsi_ops = {
